1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,670
August, sixteen sixty-six.

2
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:07,550
In the Mughal city of Agra, a ring of
guards surrounds the quarters of one man.

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,240
One letter from Agra puts
the watch at a thousand men.

4
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:15,710
Inside are a Maratha ruler from the
Deccan and his nine-year-old son.

5
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,980
Then, one morning, word
spreads through the city.

6
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:20,310
They are gone.

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:25,350
How do you disappear from under the eyes
of one of the richest empires on earth?

8
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:28,240
The famous answer involves
baskets of sweets.

9
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:33,130
But letters written in Agra that very
summer let us check the legend against the

10
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:34,070
record.

11
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,070
The ruler was Shivaji, the Maratha leader
who had carved a kingdom out of the hill

12
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:40,250
forts of western India,

13
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:43,350
and who had spent years
raiding Mughal territory.

14
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:45,400
The emperor was Aurangzeb.

15
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:49,600
And the man who brought them face to
face was Aurangzeb's veteran general,

16
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,160
Mirza Raja Jai Singh.

17
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:56,830
In sixteen sixty-five, Jai Singh's
army closed in on Shivaji's forts.

18
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,800
Rather than lose everything,
Shivaji made a deal at Purandar.

19
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:03,090
Twenty-three forts went to the empire.

20
00:01:03,510 --> 00:01:06,390
He kept twelve, including
his stronghold of Rajgad.

21
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:08,980
Then Jai Singh pressed for something more.

22
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:12,630
Shivaji should travel north and
appear before the emperor in person.

23
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:15,520
Jai Singh swore that he
would come to no harm.

24
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:20,090
At court, his son, the prince Ram
Singh, pledged his word as well.

25
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:26,410
In March sixteen sixty-six, Shivaji left
Rajgad with his son Sambhaji and a small

26
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:27,650
but splendid escort.

27
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:29,720
In May, they reached Agra.

28
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,860
One of Ram Singh's officers
described him in a letter home.

29
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:35,750
Lean, short, fair, bearded.

30
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:38,950
And, he wrote, "even without
finding out who he is,

31
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:42,190
one does feel instinctively
that he is a ruler of men."

32
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,380
On the twelfth of May,

33
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:47,440
the emperor's fiftieth birthday
by the lunar calendar,

34
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,290
Ram Singh led Shivaji into the fort.

35
00:01:50,950 --> 00:01:53,020
Shivaji presented his gifts of gold.

36
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:54,820
And then, nothing.

37
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:57,270
The emperor did not say a word to him.

38
00:01:57,930 --> 00:02:01,030
Shivaji was led back to stand
behind rows of other nobles.

39
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:04,380
Robes of honour were handed
out to princes and ministers,

40
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:09,510
and to Maharaja Jaswant Singh, a general
who had once besieged one of Shivaji's

41
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:10,910
forts and failed.

42
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,240
Shivaji's patience broke.

43
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:16,420
According to a letter
from Ram Singh's staff,

44
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:19,170
he told the prince, "I
cast off your mansab,"

45
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:20,360
his imperial rank.

46
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:23,340
Then he turned his back on
the throne and walked away.

47
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:26,240
At a court where nobles
were expected to wait,

48
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:29,140
as an English trader put it,
"with their hands before them,

49
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:32,080
like mutes," it was a
stunning act of defiance.

50
00:02:32,830 --> 00:02:34,330
Officials brought him a robe of honour.

51
00:02:34,690 --> 00:02:35,590
He refused it.

52
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,690
The backlash was swift.

53
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:41,650
Powerful voices at court, the
emperor's sister Jahanara among them,

54
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:42,950
demanded punishment.

55
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:46,780
A letter from Agra reports that the
emperor weighed killing Shivaji,

56
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,710
or locking him away in a fortress.

57
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:50,290
Ram Singh stepped in.

58
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:52,970
His father had guaranteed
Shivaji's safety,

59
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:53,940
he argued.

60
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:57,510
If the emperor wanted Shivaji dead,
he should kill Ram Singh first.

61
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,480
The emperor's reply was simple.

62
00:03:00,050 --> 00:03:01,480
Then sign a security bond.

63
00:03:01,850 --> 00:03:04,090
If Shivaji escapes, you
will answer for it.

64
00:03:05,050 --> 00:03:06,220
Ram Singh signed.

65
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:09,770
Shivaji was not executed,
but he was not free.

66
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:12,720
At one point he was
ordered to march to Kabul,

67
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,780
on the far north-western frontier.

68
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:18,440
Days later, after petitions
and payments to courtiers,

69
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:19,660
the order was dropped.

70
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:22,900
Troops of the city's
police chief, Fulad Khan,

71
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:24,330
ringed his quarters.

72
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:27,460
Ram Singh's own Rajputs
watched his bed at night.

73
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:30,190
The emperor's guest had
become his prisoner.

74
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:32,450
Shivaji tried everything.

75
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:35,370
He offered two crore
rupees, twenty million,

76
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:36,710
if his forts were returned.

77
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:40,260
He offered to go and fight for
the emperor against Bijapur.

78
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,510
He asked to be moved to another house.

79
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:46,150
He even asked to go to Benares
and become a holy man.

80
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:49,550
The reply came back:
let him become a fakir,

81
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:52,340
and live in Allahabad fort, under guard.

82
00:03:53,550 --> 00:03:56,730
Then came a blow from the man
who had promised his safety.

83
00:03:57,300 --> 00:04:00,140
In July, Jai Singh wrote to
his son from the Deccan.

84
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,330
His war there was going badly, and it was,

85
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:06,700
he said, "not at all politic"
to let Shivaji come home.

86
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:09,220
Keep him in Agra, he advised.

87
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,470
Treat him well, but keep him.

88
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,540
By now Shivaji's money was running low.

89
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,850
He borrowed sixty-six thousand
rupees from Ram Singh.

90
00:04:18,810 --> 00:04:21,200
And over the summer he
sent his own escort home,

91
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,320
leaving himself almost alone.

92
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:25,740
To the court, it looked like surrender.

93
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,550
It was preparation.

94
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,160
Shivaji fell ill, or appeared to.

95
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:33,380
Large baskets of sweets
began to leave his quarters,

96
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:36,490
gifts for Brahmins,
holy men and courtiers.

97
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:40,100
Each was slung from a pole
and carried by two porters.

98
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:43,580
At first, the guards opened
them, and found sweets.

99
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:46,340
After some days, they
stopped opening them.

100
00:04:47,650 --> 00:04:50,370
Then, one evening in the
third week of August,

101
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:51,970
the plan went into motion.

102
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:55,590
According to later accounts,
Shivaji's half-brother,

103
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:59,880
Hiroji Farzand, lay down on
Shivaji's bed beneath a quilt,

104
00:05:00,230 --> 00:05:03,900
with one arm showing, and Shivaji's
gold bracelet on the wrist.

105
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:07,400
A boy sat by the bed, massaging his feet.

106
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:11,500
And inside the baskets, among
others filled with real sweets,

107
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:13,810
crouched Shivaji and his son.

108
00:05:15,470 --> 00:05:17,290
The porters carried them past the guards,

109
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:18,880
and out into the dark.

110
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,520
How long did the trick hold?

111
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:25,060
The chronicles say the guards were
fooled for most of the next day,

112
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:28,850
until the house fell strangely
quiet and they found the bed empty.

113
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:31,910
The contemporary letters
suggest it was quicker.

114
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:35,290
One, written in Agra and dated
the eighteenth of August,

115
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:38,720
says simply, "This morning
Shivaji was found to have fled."

116
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:40,860
The city erupted.

117
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:45,730
Ram Singh's own staff wrote home urging
that every pass and river crossing be

118
00:05:45,770 --> 00:05:50,750
watched, and that anyone dressed as a yogi
or a sannyasi be questioned and searched.

119
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:53,710
Fulad Khan, whose men
had ringed the house,

120
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:57,000
told the emperor the escape had happened
on Ram Singh's side of the watch.

121
00:05:57,760 --> 00:06:01,640
Ram Singh's men were seized and threatened
until they said their master had helped.

122
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:04,850
Some later took it back, saying
they had spoken out of fear.

123
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:09,590
The emperor, angry, cut Ram Singh's
rank and took away his lands.

124
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:12,040
So, was it really the baskets?

125
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:16,410
About two weeks after the escape, one of
Ram Singh's officers wrote that the trick

126
00:06:16,450 --> 00:06:17,350
had become known.

127
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:20,880
Shivaji had slipped out "by
crouching down in the baskets."

128
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:23,980
Later Mughal and Maratha
histories tell the same story.

129
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:27,060
But the Mughal court suspected
inside help as well.

130
00:06:27,670 --> 00:06:30,280
And a European writer of the
period, Niccolao Manucci,

131
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:32,850
claimed that Ram Singh himself
had quietly arranged it.

132
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,610
With frightened guards
and partisan witnesses,

133
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:38,140
we may never know exactly
who looked the other way.

134
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,010
What happened next grew into legend.

135
00:06:41,530 --> 00:06:45,130
For generations, Shivaji's flight
was told as a long pilgrimage,

136
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:50,090
through Benares, Gaya, even Puri,
full of narrow escapes in disguise.

137
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:54,890
The chronicles say he smeared himself with
ash and travelled as a wandering ascetic.

138
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:59,390
Then, in nineteen thirty-nine, letters
were found in the Jaipur archives.

139
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:04,360
Spy reports quoted in them said Shivaji
reached his fort just twenty-five days

140
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,680
after slipping out of Agra.

141
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:10,690
The historian Jadunath Sarkar, who had
once told the long version himself,

142
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,260
now called those pilgrimage
stories fiction.

143
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:16,800
Twenty-five days, over more
than a thousand kilometres,

144
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,590
meant hard, fast travel on hidden paths.

145
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:20,970
It cost him.

146
00:07:21,130 --> 00:07:23,050
He lay ill for weeks after he got home.

147
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,470
And Sambhaji?

148
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,520
Maratha accounts say the boy
was left behind in Mathura,

149
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,550
with a trusted Brahmin family.

150
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:36,690
The spy reports that reached the emperor
even said that Shivaji's son had died on

151
00:07:36,730 --> 00:07:37,630
the road.

152
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:39,490
That rumour may have protected him.

153
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:43,300
Months later, Sambhaji
travelled home in disguise,

154
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:46,420
passed off as a young relative
of the family sheltering him.

155
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,780
The escape changed the
course of the Deccan wars.

156
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:56,220
Within four years, Shivaji was retaking
the forts he had surrendered at Purandar.

157
00:07:57,170 --> 00:08:01,820
In sixteen seventy-four, he was
crowned Chhatrapati at Raigad.

158
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:05,290
And in a collection of sayings
attributed to Aurangzeb,

159
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:08,760
the emperor laments that
one moment of carelessness,

160
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,450
the flight of Shivaji,

161
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:14,620
dragged him into campaigns that
lasted to the end of his days.

162
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:16,600
And Ram Singh?

163
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:20,470
The prince who paid for the escape
with his rank was later sent east,

164
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:22,520
to lead a Mughal army into Assam.

165
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:26,920
There, in sixteen seventy-one,
on the Brahmaputra at Saraighat,

166
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:30,300
he faced an Ahom general
named Lachit Borphukan.

167
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:32,560
That is a story for another episode.
